A `SelectPanel` is used when the user needs to select one or more items from a list. It combines a trigger button with a dropdown panel containing searchable, selectable items.
The ability to search for items is what mainly separates this from the `ActionMenu` in our usage.

For details on the component, please see the [Primer documentation](https://primer.style/product/components/select-panel/).

## With footer button

When selections need to be explicitly confirmed before taking effect, add a footer with an action button.
The button should ideally be named "Apply".

<%= embed Patterns::SelectPanelPreview, :footer_buttons, panels: %i[source] %>

## With grouped items

Use groups when the items fall into a small number of categories that help the user decide.
An example is the role selector of the workflow editor. It shows the roles that have transitions first, and the roles without transitions after them.

Each group starts with a divider that has a short label. Put the most relevant group first.

<%= embed Patterns::SelectPanelPreview, :grouped_items, panels: %i[source] %>

### Add dividers

`Primer::Alpha::SelectPanel` does not expose `with_divider`, but its inner `ActionList` supports it.
Use a subclass that delegates `with_divider` to the list, such as `Workflows::RoleSelectPanelComponent`:

```ruby
class RoleSelectPanelComponent < Primer::Alpha::SelectPanel
  delegate :with_divider, to: :@list
end
```

Add each divider, then the items of its group. Do not add a divider for an empty group.

### Filter the items

The local filter of the panel matches the text content of an item. Set `data-filter-string` on each item, so that the filter matches the label only.

The panel does not hide a divider when the filter hides all items of its group.
To hide the empty groups, mark each divider and each item with the same group key,
and listen to the `input` event of the panel:

```ruby
panel.with_divider(data: { "admin--workflow-role-select-target": "groupHeading", role_group: index }) { label }
panel.with_item(label: role.name, item_id: role.id, data: { filter_string: role.name, role_group: index })
```

```typescript
filterGroups() {
  queueMicrotask(() => {
    const panel = this.element as SelectPanelElement;
    const visibleGroups = new Set(panel.visibleItems.map((item) => item.dataset.roleGroup));
    this.groupHeadingTargets.forEach((heading) => {
      heading.style.display = visibleGroups.has(heading.dataset.roleGroup) ? 'flex' : 'none';
    });
  });
}
```

The `queueMicrotask` call makes sure that the panel has updated its visible items before the controller reads them.
The preview above uses the `admin--workflow-role-select` controller. Type "read" in the filter to see the "With transitions" group disappear.

